  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe plain hop between two runs of `emit_runs` (`crates/motion/src/finishing3d/march.rs`) changed:\n\n- The hop plane is `max(retract, next run start, current run end)`. Before, the end of the current run was not in the formula.\n- The move across is made at that plane only if the plane is at or above the highest facet of the model, or if `gaplink::straight_ok` (the exact sweep) clears the move. If not, the hop goes to the clearance plane.\n- When the retract plane (or clearance) is at or above the model top, the hop is the same as before, move for move. No sweep runs in that case.\n\nThe decision is in `docs/decisions/3627-finish-hop-height.md`. The sentence in `docs/decisions/3362-pass-start-finish3d.md` that said each link \"is certified by the existing laws\" has a correction.\n\n## The three answers (on main 7c637d705, before the fix)\n\nFixture: a stepped pocket (top at z 10, floor at z 5), Contour, BN-0600 (r 3), retract 7.\n\n1. Reachable: yes. No rule refuses a retract plane below the top of the part. `sane.rs` and the height resolver check only that the value is finite. MCP `edit_operation` accepts it and `generate` gives status `ok`.\n2. The tool goes into the part: yes.\n3. The verifier blocks the post: yes. Findings: `rapid_in_stock`, `envelope` 3.0 mm gouge, `post_gate` gouge in 171 cells (worst 3.00 mm). `held_by: [\"F1\"]`. Nothing passed silently, so the coordinator set the priority to P3.\n\n## Moves of the hop\n\nBefore:\n- Feed to (7.352, -7.352, 10.0) (end of the last top pass)\n- Feed down to (7.352, -7.352, 7.0) (into the part)\n- Rapid to (2.705, -2.705, 7.0) (through the block)\n\nAfter:\n- Feed to (7.352, -7.352, 10.0)\n- Rapid to (2.705, -2.705, 10.0)\n- Plunge to (2.705, -2.705, 5.0)\n\n## Pins\n\nEach new pin is red on the old `march.rs` and green with the fix (checked by a local revert of `march.rs`):\n- `camcraft-motion` `finish3d_hop_height`:\n  - `a_retract_below_the_high_run_never_takes_the_tool_into_the_part` (cavity, Contour, verifier clean)\n  - `inside_first_on_a_convex_part_with_a_low_retract_never_digs_in` (mesa, `contour_from(.., PassStart::Inside)`, #3362)\n  - `a_retract_above_the_part_hops_clean` (retract None and 15: clean, unchanged)\n- `camcraft-motion` lib `finishing3d::hop_tests` (drives `emit_runs` directly):\n  - `high_run_first_with_a_low_retract_never_digs_into_the_mesa`\n  - `a_retract_below_a_ridge_between_the_runs_goes_over_it`\n  - `a_retract_above_the_part_is_the_plain_hop` (exact old moves)\n- `camcraft-app` `finish3d_hop_height` (MCP import, edit, generate, verify):\n  - `a_retract_below_the_top_of_the_part_is_accepted_and_verifies_clean`\n  - `the_default_hop_verifies_clean`\n\nNote: on the mesa with `Inside`, the verifier still gives `RapidInStock` for the hops between the base passes at z 7. The verifier reads the stock as uncut up to its top (z 10). That is its own conservative law and not this hop. The test asserts that each such rapid is above the base and off the mesa, and that no other blocking finding occurs.\n\n## Gate (final head, debug, -j 6)\n\n- motion: `--lib` (551 ok), `finish3d`, `finish3d_gaplink`, `finish3d_holes`, `finish3d_land`, `finish3d_overhang_and_chord`, `finish3d_pass_start`, `scallop_ceiling`, `multiaxis`, `finish3d_hop_height`: all ok. `cargo test -p camcraft-motion --no-run`: ok.\n- app: `--lib` (300 ok), `golden_cl`, `conformance`, `verify`, `shared_face_bodies_finish`, `finish3d_direction`, `operations`, `example_catalog`, `example_catalog_adaptive`, `example_catalog_edge_work`, `first_part_programs`, `finish3d_hop_height`: all ok. The goldens did not change.\n- clippy `-D warnings`: motion `--all-targets` ok; app `--lib --test finish3d_hop_height` ok.\n\n## Not run\n\n- No heavy lane and no light lane. The issue is P3, so it gets no heavy step.\n- The rings' hop (`rings.rs`) did not change. It already lifts its plane to the ring level.\n\nChangelog: 3D Finish: a hop between passes with a retract height below the end of the pass no longer feeds the tool down into the part; it stays at the pass height when the move across is clear, else it goes to the clearance height.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #3627\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
